# Template Conformance (Vecinita)

Vecinita is a **hybrid monorepo** (DO apps + Modal apps + shared packages). Do **not**
apply the CogniChem antibody Job template (`cognichem-rfantibody`, single `src/app.py`
pipeline). That overlay was leftover and is retired for this repo (S031).

[Corpus: architecture] [Corpus: deploy-integration] [Spec: docs/adr/ADR-037-unified-vecinita-llm-modal-app.md]

## Monorepo layout (required)

```
apps/
  chat-rag-backend/
  chat-rag-frontend/
  data-management-backend/
  data-management-frontend/
  internal-write-api/
  database/
packages/
  rag/ ingest/ embedding-client/ llm-client/ tagging/ eval/
  shared-schemas/ frontend-i18n/ frontend-ui/
infra/
  modal/          # Modal app modules
  do/             # App Platform YAML (SECRET placeholders only)
tests/            # unit, e2e, integration, privacy, smoke, eval, bugs, ui
```

Surface `[Template Drift]` if a new top-level deployable appears without architecture /
CORPUS updates.

## Modal patterns (Vecinita)

| App | Module | Role |
|-----|--------|------|
| `vecinita-embedding` | `infra/modal/embedding_app.py` | Multilingual embed |
| `vecinita-data-management` | `infra/modal/data_management_app.py` | ASGI + ingest/automation workers |
| `vecinita-llm` | `infra/modal/llm_app.py` | Prod ChatRAG / ingest vLLM |
| `vecinita-llm-playground` | `infra/modal/llm_playground_app.py` | Admin/eval sandbox |
| `vecinita-llm-finetune` | `infra/modal/finetune_app.py` | LoRA/PEFT train (F77) |

- Prefer **Modal-agnostic core** under `apps/` / `packages/` with thin Modal wiring in
  `infra/modal/`.
- Prod vs playground LLM URLs stay separate ([unified-vecinita-llm.mdc](unified-vecinita-llm.mdc)).
- F75/F76 share **one** schedule with distinct `job_type`s (ADR-052).
- F77 adapters load on prod **only after human promote** (ADR-053).

## DigitalOcean

- Four App Platform specs under `infra/do/` — never commit live operator `*-spec.yaml`
  exports with encrypted secrets.
- Only DO backends may hold `DATABASE_URL`.

## When drift is acceptable

Template drift that matches a new ADR / feature is fine:
1. Explain the rationale
2. Update `docs/architecture.md` + CORPUS as needed
3. Update this rule if the deviation becomes the new convention
